course: dictionary
lesson: 7076
title: Sounds, feet and sales talk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one fits. Read the words around it for clues. «The patter of rain on the tin roof kept everyone awake.» Rain makes a soft tapping sound, so patter means a quick, light tapping sound here. Then check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «Then the pattering began.» This does not say what is pattering, so read on. The next line says «the pat-pat-pat of little feet», so the clue tells you the meaning. Clues can come after the word as well as before it.
explain: Patter can also be fast, clever talk. A salesman's patter is quick talk that tries to make you buy something. In «The Wind in the Willows», Toad comes pattering after his friends: here patter means moving with quick, light steps. Same word, three meanings, and only the context tells you which one you need.
fact: Patter can be a noun (the patter of rain) or a verb (rain pattering on the roof).
fact: «Patter» means a quick, light, tapping sound, like rain or small feet.
fact: «Patter» can also mean fast, clever talk, such as a salesman's sales patter.
fact: In Scotland, informal «patter» means chat and jokes: «He's got great patter.»
fact: Sales patter can trick you into buying, so listen carefully to what is really being said.
exercise: «The patter of rain on the tin roof kept everyone awake.» What does patter mean here? | *A quick, light tapping sound | A heavy, slow walk | A sweet, warm drink | A loud crash of thunder
exercise: «The salesman's patter made the old kettle sound like a bargain.» What does patter mean here? | A slow way of walking | *Fast, clever talk used to sell something | A sleepy song | A soft tapping sound on a window
exercise: «Toad came pattering after them.» Find and copy the word that shows quick, light steps. | them | came | *pattering | Toad
test: Which meaning of patter fits best in «the patter of tiny feet»? | A big, shaking room | *A quick, light tapping sound | Fast, clever talk | A slow, heavy march
test: A Scottish friend says, «He's got great patter.» What does patter mean? | A tapping sound on glass | A kind of bird | *Chat and jokes | A heavy coat
exam: Why does the writer use patter in «the pat-pat-pat of little feet»? | To say the feet are far away | *To help the reader hear a soft tapping sound | To show the feet are angry | To tell the reader it is night
